camchrome: an Android persona rasterises at (nearly) its devicePixelRatio, with an exact viewport.

1008 sized a phone persona's window but left the raster scale at 1x, so the Clearcote audit row
"devicePixelRatio is the scale layout actually rasterises at" stayed (a 100 px box measured 100
device pixels at a reported 2.625). Forcing 2.625 itself made X11 round the window to 1082 px and
the viewport to 413 CSS px. The browser now forces floor(width x dpr) / width (412 at 2.625 ->
1081/412): the window is exactly 1081 px, the content area exactly 412 CSS px, and a 100 px box
measures 262.4 device pixels, within the one pixel of rounding a fractional-ratio display has. The
reported devicePixelRatio stays the persona's; an explicit --force-device-scale-factor wins. The X
screen must hold the phone at that scale: tools/persona_display.py sizes it so.

--- a/chrome/app/chrome_main_delegate.cc
+++ b/chrome/app/chrome_main_delegate.cc
@@ -7,6 +7,9 @@
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX)
 #include <sched.h>
 #endif
+#include <cmath>
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX)
+#endif
 
 #include <stddef.h>
 
@@ -1262,6 +1265,23 @@
                                base::NumberToString(persona.screen_width) + "," +
                                    base::NumberToString(persona.screen_height));
       }
+      // camchrome (1017): and it rasterises at (nearly) its devicePixelRatio. A page measures
+      // the raster scale (ResizeObserver device-pixel-content-box, srcset), which stayed 1x.
+      // X11 windows are whole pixels, so the scale is chosen to make the phone's width a
+      // whole number of them: floor(width x dpr) / width (412 at 2.625 -> 1081/412 = 2.6238).
+      // The content area stays exactly the phone's width, a 100 px box measures within one
+      // device pixel of 100 x dpr (as a fractional-ratio display rounds), and the reported
+      // devicePixelRatio stays the persona's. Needs an X screen of the phone's size at that
+      // scale; tools/persona_display.py starts one. An explicit scale factor wins.
+      if (persona.mobile && persona.screen_width > 0 &&
+          persona.device_pixel_ratio > 1.0 &&
+          !cmd->HasSwitch(switches::kForceDeviceScaleFactor)) {
+        const double physical =
+            std::floor(persona.screen_width * persona.device_pixel_ratio);
+        const double scale = physical / persona.screen_width;
+        cmd->AppendSwitchASCII(switches::kForceDeviceScaleFactor,
+                               base::NumberToString(scale));
+      }
       // Phones run Google Chrome: a "Chromium"-only brand list with no plugins is the
       // Chrome for Testing / headless signature on Android. An explicit brand wins.
